# Byte-exact fixtures.
#
# These files are consumed as raw bytes: a zstd frame is fed to a decoder, and a
# CAS blob is keyed by the digest of its own content. Any EOL conversion silently
# corrupts them, and the resulting test failure points at the decoder or the hash
# rather than at git. Mark them binary so no conversion is ever applied.

*.zst binary

# Content-addressed blob fixtures: filename is the blake3 of the file's bytes.
engine/commands/fixtures/blob-layout-v1/** binary
**/fixtures/**/blake3/** binary

# JSON fixtures are deliberately left as text — nothing hashes them bytewise,
# and readable diffs are worth more than the uniformity.
